  "summary": "CT list for St. Brigid Imaging, Mon 10/26: 4 booked studies (appts 00001, 00006 and 00008 were cancelled and left alone). One CT order placed per booked study, linked to its appointment.\n\n1. pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0001). Diabetic; last creatinine (9/24) was more than 30 days before the scan, so I ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0005). Later, outside results showed creatinine 1.04 → 1.52 between 10/21 and 10/22, which is acute kidney injury. I added NS 500 mL IV at 07:00 (mr-t0021), kept the pre-scan creatinine, and sent the patient corrected instructions (comm-t0026). Follow-up task created (task-t0034).\n\n2. pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0002). The 2019 radiology report grades his iohexol reaction as moderate. The allergy list's \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\" does not change that grade, so I ordered §2 premedication: prednisone 50 mg Sun 20:00, Mon 02:00 and 08:00 (mr-t0007), and diphenhydramine 50 mg Mon 08:00 (mr-t0008). Later, his 10/14 creatinine was corrected to 2.8 (the first value came from another patient's sample), giving an eGFR of about 24. I added NS 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0022). Spanish/English instructions went out (comm-t0013), then a correction (comm-t0025) withdrawing the \"normal kidneys\" statement. He needs a driver. Follow-up task created (task-t0033).\n\n3. pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0003). She had AKI at the ED on 10/04 and her creatinine was not back to baseline. I ordered a pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0006) and NS 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0009). I put metformin (mr-00392) on hold, ordered a creatinine 48 hours after the scan (sr-t0011), and created a restart-review task (task-t0012). That task's text cites sr-t0007 by mistake; the right order is sr-t0011, as noted in the chart. A late outside report shows a moderate reaction to iopamidol in 2022, so I added premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0023) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0024). Messages sent: comm-t0015, then the correction comm-t0027. She needs a driver. The iopamidol allergy could not be coded in the allergy list, so it is flagged in the note for manual entry.\n\n4. pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT A/P without contrast (sr-t0004), ordered as booked; no prep needed (comm-t0016). A late report of a mild iohexol reaction in 2024 does not change a non-contrast study. I added it to the allergy list (alg-t0028).\n\nNotes and addenda citing RBC-RAD-07 are written for each patient. All 4 new inbox items are completed and linked. Pre-existing inbox items for other patients were not touched.",
